// <vector> as seen through the Dinkum C++ Library 2.33. RECONSTRUCTION.
// Base: the stock VC6 <vector> (Dinkum 2.x lineage: member names, layout allocator/_First/_Last/_End).
// Changed to what the AoC binaries prove (TCP Protocol.dll addresses):
//  - iterators are _Ptrit class objects, not raw pointers (0x3364 begin, 0x3370 end, 0x3558, 0x3750)
//  - construction goes through _Buy(0) (0x100a -> 0x36e1); _Buy has no max_size check (0x36e1)
//  - destruction goes through _Tidy (0x3718: destroy, deallocate, zero all three pointers)
//  - clear() is erase(begin(), end()), out of line (0x3329)
//  - erase(first, last) is guarded by first != last and copies to a raw pointer (0x3514 -> copy 0x42e6)
//  - _Ufill carries the library's try/catch-all rollback (_Destroy of the partial range). Without /GX the
//    _TRY macros leave a dead `if (0) {...}` block that still counts against VC6's inline budget, which is what
//    makes insert(P, M, X) call _Construct out of line (TCP 0x44aa/0x44bb/0x44cd, mixer 0x21ee) and call the
//    second _Ufill out of line for class elements (TCP 0x41c5/0x4275). probes/inline_ufill_try.cpp
//  - insert(P, M, X)'s grow branch copies under its own try/catch-all (_Destroy(_S, _Q) + deallocate, the later
//    Dinkum _Insert_n shape). The dead block is what lets the old-array destroy loop inline the element's
//    implicit dtor (LLE 0x2f8d ESChecksumEntry, Default 0x63e2/0x66c6/0x9fba/0xa8bc/0x13ccb) and keeps the
//    dead stores of an empty-dtor loop (LLE 0x24b50 GERectangle). Without it: ??_G(0) calls.
//  - constructors are the later Dinkum overload set over a _Vector_val<_Ty, _A> base holding the allocator
//    (_Vector_val(_A _Al = _A())), not VC6's default arguments: vector() builds its own allocator temporary
//    (LLE UIFileComboBox 0x6f94b and NESynchronousServer 0x4a067 are out-of-line ctors that take no argument and
//    copy the allocator byte from an uninitialised slot of their own frame). The base, not a member initialised
//    from _A(), is the better fit module-wide (GETextureSet ctor 0x346a7 exact only with it). Same shape as sxlrt233's exported
//    _String_val(allocator) with its ??_F default closure and basic_string()/basic_string(const _A&) pair.
//  - reserve(N): max_size check -> _Xlen, then _Ucopy(begin(), end(), _S) under a try/catch-all and the old
//    array destroyed + freed under one _First != 0 check (LLE U2DSparseArray 0x557b4)
//  - member template insert(P, F, L) -> _Insert(P, F, L, _Iter_cat(F)) (exe 0x96506 / 0x96854, deque iterators):
//    the insert(P, M, X) grow shape with _Ucopy(F, L); spill branch _Ucopy(P, end(), P + M), advance(_Mid,
//    end() - _P), _Ucopy(_Mid, _L, _Last), _Last += _M, copy(_F, _Mid, _P); else (0 < _M) _Ucopy of the tail,
//    copy_backward, copy. It is the only range insert: exe 0x6bd85 (insert over vector iterators) forwards to the same
//    _Insert (0x40140), and VC6 calls a non-template const_iterator overload beside it ambiguous
//  - assign(F, L) is a member template -> _Assign(F, L, _Iter_cat(F)) = erase(begin(), end()) + insert(begin(), F, L)
//    (exe 0x92230 / 0x926d6), as in <list>
// Members not yet proven keep the VC6 shapes, rewritten over pointers. vector<bool> is not reconstructed.
